ences both new and old  alike it tells an unbelievable story  that intertwines real world of  from the 1980s with loads of melodrama  fantastical characters and an offbeat  sense of humor you slip into the boots  of a super soldier with a tragic  backstory and an army at his command who  must face impossible odds while sneaking  behind enemy lines the phantom pain has  a massive world that's been crafted with  an incredible attention to detail which  is reflected in the interplay of  numerous mechanics the artificial  intelligence and the flexibility of the  emergent gameplay moments that await you  at every turn the phantom pain is the  Metal Gear series is missing link and  while not everyone is pleased by the way  Kajima tied things together he certainly  managed to do what he does best deliver  a story that subverts expectations  redefining the truth and your  understanding of the series at large we  gave the phantom pain a 10 in our review  not because it's a perfect game but  because it offers an essential  experience that we think everyone should  try
 

